The attached image (Figure 3 from npj Vaccines, 2017) illustrates that Nano-11 induces a transient inflammatory response at the injection site and is taken up by recruited cells. Panel A, a line graph, shows the kinetics of various inflammatory cell types, including neutrophils, macrophages, antigen-presenting cells, eosinophils, and monocytes, at the injection site over 21 days following Nano-11 administration. Neutrophils and Mac-2+ macrophages peak at day 2, while antigen-presenting cells increase through day 2, and all cell numbers largely diminish by day 21. Panel B presents confocal microscopy images at different time points, demonstrating the presence of fluorescently labeled Nano-11 within MHCII+, Ly6C+, and Mac-2+ cells, indicating uptake by macrophages and dendritic cells. This highlights Nano-11's ability to recruit immune cells and be internalized, supporting its role as a vaccine adjuvant.